format session-log-v1
stamp 20260820.082858
editor Claude Code
model claude-opus-5
voice Kyri
host Vultr SEA NixOS VPS ai-jail pier (Daylight DC-1 hand) -- Eastern (EDT)
title Caravan heed -- a plan run under a quarrel it inherited says so
prompt Keaton set the loop running: be Kyri in Radiant Style, read the operator card and the itineraries, close open agent-closable reds first, take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, deep-read one council-rota doc, condense REMEMBER, and send each finished increment as its own signed round.
think Standfast first. Every living row in crux/REDS.md reads CLOSED -- %96 and %97 closed with duty 5 and the prose-shape scan, %81 with the count guard bijection, %83 with the ASCII loom, %84 on measurement. No open agent-closable red stood, so the line was clear for new work.
think The running thread came from the newest log's recommend, not from REMEMBER alone. endure had just landed: a pressed quarrel now outlives the run that heard it, and the recommend named exactly what it left open -- the next run opens knowing somebody presses still, and nothing obliges it to do anything about that, so a quarrel can stand forever in a note every run reads and no run answers.
think The crux, then, is what a run owes a position it inherits. The honest answer is small, and naming its smallness is what made the rung buildable: a supervisor cannot settle a quarrel and cannot withdraw one. What it can do is refuse to publish its outcome as though the quarrel were not there.
think So the measurement chose itself -- plans reported carried while an inherited quarrel stood against them. It falls 1 to 0, and the price is one byte beside a settlement the run had already published.
think The structural finding arrived while placing the step. Every rung of this arc runs at the end of a run, and endure writes plan.standing last of all. A plan reading that note after its own work would sometimes be reading its own handwriting back as somebody else's judgment. So the heeding reads the standing note as the first act after provisioning and publishes only at the end -- the first rung of the arc whose two halves face opposite ends of the run.
think The lap's reader was written to accept, on purpose. A reader who pressed would leave this run carrying a position of its own, and the regard could then be read as an answer to that one rather than to the inherited quarrel. Accepting makes the finding unambiguous: nothing this run heard itself could account for the regard it publishes.
think Regard clears with the findings and never with the position -- a quarrel belongs to the person holding it, a word about that quarrel belongs to the run that said it. That seam is proven as its own fold, since no single run can show it from inside itself.
obs The word is never softened. Both runs settle carried out whole; a run that quietly settled short because somebody objected would let a quarrel decide what the work came to. The regard adds company, not doubt.
obs The generalization lap runs first rather than last this time, so the wire an operator reads at the end of the selftest is the wire the finding itself left there -- plan.settled c, plan.standing p, plan.appeal a, plan.regard u. The rung in miniature, readable in four cats.
obs Four refusals stand by name -- HeedEarly the moment, HeedUnpressed the hard half, HeedMiscounted the count, HeedMisrecorded the record. Reaching HeedEarly on the wire took disarming both counts first, because the subtraction in unweighed_in overflows before the refusal can fire. The arithmetic was doing its job, and the honest note says so rather than hiding it.
obs The planted control is the one worth keeping: with the note never written, the read-back skipped, the wire fold's read and the harness read all disarmed, the selftest prints GREEN while plan.regard holds only the provisioning's zero byte. An operator would read a clean outcome over a live quarrel while the run reported it heeded. Seeing that once is what makes the reading back a check rather than decoration.
obs rota doc this lap was item 16, SIMPLE_LOVABLE_COMPLETE, taken as choir count 70 mod 27. Its three questions bounded the rung honestly: simple, since the whole addition is one enum, one note, and one supervisor step; lovable, since the four notes read as a sentence; complete, since the loop closes -- the position is read, weighed, published, read back, and left standing for its holder.
loom witness=caravan_heed_witness rungs_green=70 refusals=4 red_paths=5 measurement_from=1 measurement_to=0
file caravan/heed.rye the rung -- Heed and Regard, the folds, the regard note, and weigh_the_standing, delegating every elder fold to endure.rye
file tools/caravan_heed_witness.rish the witness on metal -- the finding, the two-run lap, the wire reads, and the five RED paths named
file tools/caravan_suite_witness.rish registers heed in the choir; the bijection guard now sings 70
file caravan/README.md the durable per-rung record -- roster row and the heed section
file crux/REMEMBER.md live edge moved to heed; endure and appeal condensed to one pointer so the card stays single-stranded
recommend keep-going the arc now corrects a record, carries the correction, hears the answer, records the disagreement, escorts the word, bounds the objection, stands its standing, tells the raiser, reads their reply, carries a live quarrel past the run that heard it, and finally makes the run that inherits one answer for it in its own word -- so the question above it is what an operator does with that word: the regard is published and read, and nothing in the arc lets the person reading it act, which means a plan can stand honestly qualified forever while the quarrel it names goes nowhere.
